      "script": "My boss denied everything. He gave verbal instructions in meetings, then blamed me when the result matched exactly what he asked for. So I started to send a written recap after every conversation: task, deadline, and his approval. He rejected every one with “too much email,” but never corrected a detail. Three months later, the quarterly audit arrived and found a project he claimed I had changed without permission. He called me into a conference room with HR and began explaining my “pattern.” I opened the entire paper trail. Every recap showed his instructions, and every message showed him reading it without objection. HR asked whether he had any written correction. He had none. The project stayed with me, the warning disappeared, and his new performance plan required all changes in writing. Apparently email was only excessive until it became evidence.",
